   "text": "I read the molecule region by region, from the left of the drawing to the right.\n\n1. **Indazole:** a 2H-indazole with N and NH drawn at the top. The benzo ring carries a 1-methylcyclopropyl ether (O\u2013C(CH3)(CH2CH2)) at C5, and C3 is bonded to the pyrimidine.\n2. **Pyrimidine:** C4 is attached to the indazole and C6 to the piperidine nitrogen.\n3. **Piperidine:** N-linked to the pyrimidine, with an ether oxygen at C4.\n4. **Cyclobutane:** 1,3-disubstituted. The ether oxygen is on a hashed bond and the CH2 to the piperazine is on a bold wedge, so the two substituents are trans.\n5. **Piperazine:** a CH2 on one nitrogen, and the other nitrogen is bonded to the isoindolinone ring.\n6. **Isoindolinone:** a lactam C=O, with the lactam N bearing the glutarimide (2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl). Fluorine is on the aromatic carbon next to the piperazine-bearing carbon and next to the CH2-bearing ring-fusion carbon.\n\nI assigned the two cyclobutane stereocentres from the wedge/hash geometry as [C@@H] for the oxygen-bearing carbon and [C@@H] for the CH2-bearing carbon, which gives the trans arrangement drawn. The glutarimide carbon has plain bonds, so it carries no stereo label.\n\nSMILES: C1(C)(CC1)Oc1ccc2n[nH]c(c2c1)-c1cc(N2CCC(CC2)O[C@@H]2C[C@@H](CN3CCN(CC3)c3ccc4C(=O)N(C5CCC(=O)NC5=O)Cc4c3F)C2)ncn1"
